    {
      "id": 162390,
      "name": "Belle Sorciere",
      "username": "Belle_Sorciere",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/belle_sorciere/{size}/1982_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-16T01:07:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The Scholar used an Oblivaeon shard to make his philosopher's stone. He's turning his flesh literally to metal in that card, hence \"Flesh to Iron.\" That is, as a matter of transmutation. The other Oblivaeon shards we know about augmented others' powers in different ways - the Sentinels for example didn't get transmutation powers similar to the Scholar's from their Oblivaeon shards.&nbsp;</p><p>Baron Blade is wearing an invention on his arm. He did not turn his arm into metal, nor is he transmuting anything. A connection seems unlikely, and just saying they look similar isn't really enough to establish that connection. Contextually, Luminary invents things. Scholar transmutes things. They are different.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:43:12.423Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
