      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>The Scholar used an Oblivaeon shard to make his philosopher&#39;s stone. He&#39;s turning his flesh literally to metal in that card, hence &quot;Flesh to Iron.&quot; That is, as a matter of transmutation. The other Oblivaeon shards we know about augmented others&#39; powers in different ways - the Sentinels for example didn&#39;t get transmutation powers similar to the Scholar&#39;s from their Oblivaeon shards.&nbsp;</p><p>Baron Blade is wearing an invention on his arm. He did not turn his arm into metal, nor is he transmuting anything. A connection seems unlikely, and just saying they look similar isn&#39;t really enough to establish that connection. Contextually, Luminary invents things. Scholar transmutes things. They are different.</p>",
