      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Belle Sorciere\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Belle Sorciere:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The Scholar used an Oblivaeon shard to make his philosopher's stone. He's turning his flesh literally to metal in that card, hence \"Flesh to Iron.\" That is, as a matter of transmutation. The other Oblivaeon shards we know about augmented others' powers in different ways - the Sentinels for example didn't get transmutation powers similar to the Scholar's from their Oblivaeon shards.&nbsp;Baron Blade is wearing an invention on his arm. He did not turn his arm into metal, nor is he transmuting anything. A connection seems unlikely, and just saying they look similar isn't really enough to establish that connection. Contextually, Luminary invents things. Scholar transmutes things. They are different.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>They used Oblivion shards, not OblivAeon shards.&nbsp; They are spelled Oblivion every time referenced.</p>",
